windowed-mode: a "Windowed" checkbox in the launcher's configuration dialog. With it ticked, the chosen resolution is
shown in a window (with a title bar, centred on the main screen) instead of fullscreen; the mode list is unchanged.

The game's display code (the DirectX 7 sample framework) can already render in a window: a desktop-compatible device
has a width-0 "Windowed Mode" pseudo-mode, which WinMain's D3DApp filter hides. D3DApp::CreateDevice now takes that
path when the checkbox is ticked, after giving the window a title bar and the chosen mode's client size; the frame is
shown into the client area (ShowFrame's Blt), and the window procedure measures that area again when the window moves
(the game measured it once). The checkbox is saved in the launcher's registry "Setup" value, in its unused padding
(an older saved value reads as fullscreen), and is read again when the game starts with "Play".

Files: src/app/fix_windowed.h (new: the Windows functions it needs), src/app/app_main.cpp (the checkbox, its colour
on the dialog's picture, the save, WM_MOVE, ShowFrame), src/app/d3dapp.cpp (CreateDevice), src/engine/polybatcher.cpp
(Render_Present: the game shows each frame there, not through ShowFrame, and without it a window stays black).

